**`PAYMENTS_SETTLEMENT_MODE`** is a config value that sets how `chargeOrder()` writes ledger rows. Under `legacy` it writes one row per order, and under `split` it writes two. The `v412` config bundle changed it from `legacy` to `split` and was published while all four instances still ran `v411`. `v411` doesn't recognise `split`, so its `assertSettlementMode()` threw. That caused the first 500s at 14:02.

**Migration `0042_add_settlement_currency`** is a schema change to `ledger_entries` and the second step of the `v412` release job. It ran at 14:05 and, in one transaction, it:

```sql
ALTER TABLE ledger_entries ADD COLUMN settlement_currency char(3);
UPDATE ledger_entries SET settlement_currency = 'USD';
ALTER TABLE ledger_entries ALTER COLUMN settlement_currency SET NOT NULL;
```

The column has no default and is `NOT NULL`. `v411` doesn't write it, so after the migration every `v411` insert failed with a not-null violation, whatever the mode. That is why reverting the config at 14:21 and rolling back to `v411` at 14:33 didn't help. The fix was to roll forward to `v412`, which writes the column in either mode.
